+ * first touches the module, the JS thread at app start — and called
+ * getString()/edit() without catching anything. When the app's Keystore
+ * entry becomes unusable (a known Android EncryptedSharedPreferences
+ * failure: the key can no longer decrypt the stored file, or Keystore
+ * calls hang), every launch either threw an unhandled exception or blocked
+ * reading the saved login: the app sat frozen at the Welcome screen on every
+ * start (force stop did not help), and only a reinstall — new key, new
+ * file — recovered it.
